#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166677 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/id #uuid "d6a54cb2-ea48-57b1-bf2d-7aac09915159" :question/math-academy-id "e-8595" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,t,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+16}}⟨0,4,-t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & t & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}t & 4 \\\\ 4 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & t \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨(-{t}^{2}-16),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+16}⟨-({t}^{2}+16),0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166678 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/id #uuid "b2a775f5-4a27-5cba-931f-2a45db305152" :question/math-academy-id "e-8596" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at the point $t=\\pi$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\pi ) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\pi ) & =⟨1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ and $\\mathbf N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\pi ) & =T(\\pi )\\times N(\\pi ) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,-3,4⟩\\times ⟨1,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & -3 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨(0-0),-(0-4),(0-(-3))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166679 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/id #uuid "e805dcee-247b-5aa3-9856-f7bd48bd1a78" :question/math-academy-id "e-8597" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\mathbf T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf B(t) = \\mathbf T(t) \\times \\mathbf N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $\\mathbf N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf N(t)= \\dfrac{\\mathbf T'(t)}{\\|\\mathbf T'(t)\\|}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $\\mathbf{N}(t).$ To do this, we calculate $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t)^{2}+{0}^{2}+{(-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16{cos}^{2}⁡4t+16{sin}^{2}⁡4t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16({cos}^{2}⁡4t+{sin}^{2}⁡4t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize $\\mathbf T'(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩}{(\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{5}})} \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,2,\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t & 2 \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡4t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡4t-{cos}^{2}⁡4t),0-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡4t,\\,1,\\,-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡4t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486436 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e6684f7-7607-5c50-8a99-f0423b0f6cff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨0,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485852} {:answer/id #uuid "3993447f-c94c-5806-9658-5a3fd2138263" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485877} {:answer/id #uuid "76c40781-b607-5cd9-9d60-36ce71e2a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485970} {:answer/id #uuid "a5c0152b-83d2-5b8d-9343-96df53ed9b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486064} {:answer/id #uuid "cf43edcf-7e65-57a5-b57e-f9bee6b95852" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76c40781-b607-5cd9-9d60-36ce71e2a7ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485970} :answer-field/id #uuid "42dd43f0-f4c7-5c5f-9fd8-9efa733dad89" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486266}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c2c660e0-cf11-56d9-9d4f-3449a41167f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-127612" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨0,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨0,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨({sin}^{2}⁡t-(-{cos}^{2}⁡t)),-(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-0),(-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}⟨1,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486409 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c4f14ca-3d48-5056-9fc5-f1bd5f40bc3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485906} {:answer/id #uuid "91113aca-733a-5218-9d14-5cb37e780f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486027} {:answer/id #uuid "93563b9d-d97b-5267-b9af-758059d9f304" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{2},1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486029} {:answer/id #uuid "d0e3cfdb-3f14-5b5a-9247-7b0c6d95ad5c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-1,0,2t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486142} {:answer/id #uuid "f655a3a7-5b64-5157-b793-c1097fd17f9a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨0,0,t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486210}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "91113aca-733a-5218-9d14-5cb37e780f38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486027} :answer-field/id #uuid "f62014e6-f54a-5a90-8d80-ae64d3c76c60" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486343}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8bfa2936-0cfa-5b9c-b815-96a80b635940" :question/math-academy-id "q-127617" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨1,2t,0⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-2t,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨1,2t,0⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+4{t}^{2}}}⟨-2t,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 2t & 0 \\\\ -2t & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2t \\\\ -2t & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}⟨0-0,-(0-0),1+4{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1+4{t}^{2}}⟨0,0,1+4{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,0,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186371714 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "91c16ba7-737a-5731-a5db-87aa59f9a3bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371716} {:answer/id #uuid "49467939-6bd2-5cc8-8e66-ff9c3f272469" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371717} {:answer/id #uuid "fa924ac1-afe5-5c26-94e8-b613d15e59c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371718} {:answer/id #uuid "506e1a31-362b-54d8-ab5f-3d390997cf07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371719} {:answer/id #uuid "a750a149-c913-5d57-907b-cd4df32efbaa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fa924ac1-afe5-5c26-94e8-b613d15e59c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371718} :answer-field/id #uuid "9b5a45dd-79b2-5d34-ace5-9dd5c9b8534a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186371715}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "707bba32-6581-5fec-b305-ca37df62ff61" :question/math-academy-id "q-127626" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(2) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,1,2⟩, \\\\ N(2) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,2,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(2) & =T(2)\\times N(2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,1,2⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨(-1-4),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨-5,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486440 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "076372f8-106e-57e0-804d-a269c2fc2d45" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-\\sqrt{2},\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485781} {:answer/id #uuid "757938d5-ce6f-5416-961c-6ffe6161c32a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-\\sqrt{2},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485968} {:answer/id #uuid "c54c8b06-a439-54ca-a60f-361ab446e91d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486119} {:answer/id #uuid "fcc2311a-157a-542b-a6f7-94dbd06a477a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486225} {:answer/id #uuid "febb6e78-dc07-54ef-851d-b1fd5014d597" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486231}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fcc2311a-157a-542b-a6f7-94dbd06a477a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486225} :answer-field/id #uuid "411e5861-73e4-579c-a78f-046093d8a6ef" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486265}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "c8e555e8-b363-57e5-af62-374122f991ee" :question/math-academy-id "q-127694" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-1),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{(-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t)^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{25{sin}^{2}⁡5t+25{cos}^{2}⁡5t} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-5\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩}{(\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{2}})}=⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t,\\,0,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & -1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-1 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & \\operatorname{sin}⁡5t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡5t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t & -1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t-0,-({cos}^{2}⁡5t+{sin}^{2}⁡5t),0-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡5t,\\,-1,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡5t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167498 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0bba9888-420b-5177-9749-b2a2df95fa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357850} {:answer/id #uuid "5321b4d9-3b60-50aa-86d2-67d71264b404" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨2,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358469} {:answer/id #uuid "6169e31e-bcf7-5263-9af6-da6e185aa542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358599} {:answer/id #uuid "96846c65-c6eb-5c00-b01c-0fde168b7d5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,\\,\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359068} {:answer/id #uuid "d7aee3fc-9b7d-5c2c-938d-0b42025a181c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359640}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0bba9888-420b-5177-9749-b2a2df95fa99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357850} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc6b7c4a-1590-5bf4-bd80-56a591de4f1a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360346}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "553afed7-053a-5b06-8cb8-cd7b8f67d1b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96959" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨({sin}^{2}⁡t-(-{cos}^{2}⁡t)),-(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-0),(-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1fe83c22-72da-50e6-834c-b9c00e4e385f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485820} {:answer/id #uuid "2f22d5a5-4012-55e2-9f31-a82a58b92e37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485853} {:answer/id #uuid "371ce1fd-1b49-5044-b188-c4be07437ea3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485869} {:answer/id #uuid "a47da2ab-eb87-5c1e-a609-65ef7d35cb5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486060} {:answer/id #uuid "efccc9a7-cb24-5d0b-bfc7-6c5800ec814c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1fe83c22-72da-50e6-834c-b9c00e4e385f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485820} :answer-field/id #uuid "ada9aa39-633e-53ef-a441-e0ab2035bd78" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486311}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8febc0ce-a013-5227-b117-55a62f849158" :question/math-academy-id "q-98807" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,1⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,1⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ -3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 1 \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t & 3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨(0+\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),-(0+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),(3{sin}^{2}⁡t+3{cos}^{2}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486450 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f67ace8-933a-5f11-8580-3c0b81595031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+2}}⟨0,\\sqrt{2},t⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485791} {:answer/id #uuid "77ea2de2-1ab9-50aa-b4b0-a02fcc5138ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨-\\sqrt{2}t,{t}^{2},1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485973} {:answer/id #uuid "a5292bc0-d977-5fa7-82c1-38d21ef084f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨-1,\\sqrt{2}t,-{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486063} {:answer/id #uuid "ddc45ba8-ce95-5a23-96e3-f677341d0df3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2{t}^{2}+1}}⟨-\\sqrt{2}t,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486170} {:answer/id #uuid "e1e23196-82c2-5f2e-b1d2-46dccbfbb184" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{t}^{2}+1}}⟨{t}^{2},0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486178}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a5292bc0-d977-5fa7-82c1-38d21ef084f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨-1,\\sqrt{2}t,-{t}^{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486063} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e52497f-8d9b-52ce-bfb4-48b101f7c960" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486304}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da6d9860-f69d-5d57-89ed-5b37be24ddaf" :question/math-academy-id "q-99266" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨{t}^{2},\\sqrt{2}t,1⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)}⟨2t,\\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2}),-2t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨{t}^{2},\\sqrt{2}t,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)}⟨2t,\\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2}),-2t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ {t}^{2} & \\sqrt{2}t & 1 \\\\ 2t & \\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & -2t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{2}t & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2}) & -2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & 1 \\\\ 2t & -2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & \\sqrt{2}t \\\\ 2t & \\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2})\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}-\\sqrt{2}(1-{t}^{2}),-(-2{t}^{3}-2t),(\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}(1-{t}^{2})-2\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}-\\sqrt{2},2{t}^{3}+2t,-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{4}-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1)^{2}}⟨-\\sqrt{2}({t}^{2}+1),2t({t}^{2}+1),-\\sqrt{2}{t}^{2}({t}^{2}+1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}+1}⟨-1,\\sqrt{2}t,-{t}^{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166835 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6ef73a00-12f7-5818-85a9-d8b5e2582bfe" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4cb47bec-7a6f-5792-ba0d-6e5b38af9aa6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373430} {:answer/id #uuid "ff3b30d0-baff-5a1e-9320-438cb3a67392" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373431} {:answer/id #uuid "d8339d83-7333-5325-a4b4-f881c4722e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨2\\sqrt{2},0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373432} {:answer/id #uuid "80068700-acdb-51cb-9ca8-4590c1407d03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373433} {:answer/id #uuid "1ecd40c2-7430-5053-981f-1c864376a6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373434}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ecd40c2-7430-5053-981f-1c864376a6aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373434} :answer-field/id #uuid "171888e5-1a2e-5e52-943a-a78ce9e763ca" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373429}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a933436d-0584-5de5-aa04-efee8c77b6c2" :question/math-academy-id "q-99409" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩, \\\\ N(t) & =⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,0,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,0,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩\\times ⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t,0,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡3t & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t & 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t & -\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t & 0 \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =⟨0-0,-(-{cos}^{2}⁡3t-{sin}^{2}⁡3t),0-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186167543 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28828bd8-ec03-59b4-8d26-8b3e464c2850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485833} {:answer/id #uuid "58f62199-efbb-5003-b38f-1311c44d694c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨1,2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485922} {:answer/id #uuid "b6de3b5d-312f-5e9a-a40a-688e667d53b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-1,-1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486094} {:answer/id #uuid "d14bae15-857b-5c9b-9d59-85235b09badf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-1,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486146} {:answer/id #uuid "f1913509-00f4-5dea-ba75-f27bf7624bc2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨2,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "28828bd8-ec03-59b4-8d26-8b3e464c2850" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485833} :answer-field/id #uuid "6706dd19-f83f-5a69-b331-b8b66eafd0da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186166466}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "38d9f4a8-a08e-535a-9477-a86a4bf7e353" :question/math-academy-id "q-99414" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=0,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(0) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,1,1⟩, \\\\ N(0) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(0) & =T(0)\\times N(0) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨1,1,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨(0-1),-(0-(-1)),(1-(-1))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-1,-1,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362365 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11a1ae09-acc7-534d-998d-675a3a672bfe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360903} {:answer/id #uuid "36500aea-1d78-5e1e-8a4e-61225fd63f8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨2,0,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361081} {:answer/id #uuid "3c46b9db-5c5d-5ffa-a69e-c952c7bb9bc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361114} {:answer/id #uuid "d23b25e5-b525-5f64-8360-2fafe7036e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361776} {:answer/id #uuid "f8b49b66-cdf9-5bd2-8a0f-81369247e0e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{10}}⟨1,0,3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361948}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d23b25e5-b525-5f64-8360-2fafe7036e33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361776} :answer-field/id #uuid "024da017-5d31-5d75-8afa-e61bb675b2be" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36e9c863-f2ed-5c63-bcea-d3ee9076eeb8" :question/math-academy-id "q-99415" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩, \\\\ N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) & =T(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2)\\times N(\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨3,5,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{5}⟨4,0,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & 5 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}5 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨(-15-0),-(-9-16),(0-20)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25\\sqrt{2}}⟨-15,25,-20⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\sqrt{2}}⟨-3,5,-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186362368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d3a79db-d496-5533-9506-ddba2f2e68d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360954} {:answer/id #uuid "7f642486-7c50-5f59-9a1e-b49539d68a3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361405} {:answer/id #uuid "baa23e32-f72c-5329-a831-447665cb25b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361669} {:answer/id #uuid "c08bb47f-56f7-55f2-8bdb-42aeb6789b2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,-4,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361698} {:answer/id #uuid "f2ab4af3-af01-5bc5-b1ca-9c503567f82c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨-1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "baa23e32-f72c-5329-a831-447665cb25b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186361669} :answer-field/id #uuid "22732420-8d08-537c-963c-63f5aee44079" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186362011}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "be578a50-bace-5ae6-a42e-46e5c22a651d" :question/math-academy-id "q-99420" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=1,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(1) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩, \\\\ N(1) & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(1) & =T(1)\\times N(1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,2,1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{5}}⟨-4,5,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ -4 & 5\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨(-4-5),-(-4-(-4)),(10-(-8))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9\\sqrt{5}}⟨-9,0,18⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486405 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166836 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "91ea3125-c2b7-56d0-97d8-4e54b2c01524" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Specific Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent and Principal Normal"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0150dbdf-d44e-557e-8e40-9d9fdd3e0fe0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485765} {:answer/id #uuid "5f563ca2-f1b5-5f1c-aa20-5091de5462a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485929} {:answer/id #uuid "a3256280-d56a-5ea5-880f-3efd5245d92b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-2,0,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486058} {:answer/id #uuid "b94e2c73-6ffa-542f-8611-55cad68b45b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{5}⟨3,0,4⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486100} {:answer/id #uuid "fc46879a-b942-5518-b342-3988b4e15f5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486223}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f563ca2-f1b5-5f1c-aa20-5091de5462a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨-1,0,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485929} :answer-field/id #uuid "f53e6153-04c5-5452-83ee-5ea082519b93" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486340}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "818ba628-d4d7-5ed9-973b-a4ac0ea776b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-99421" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at the point $t=3,$ given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(3) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,3,4⟩, \\\\ N(3) & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,-3⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ and $N$ denote the unit tangent and principal normal, respectively." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(3) & =T(3)\\times N(3) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}⟨0,3,4⟩\\times \\frac{1}{5}⟨0,4,-3⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -3\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}⟨(-9-16),-(0-0),(0-0)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{25}⟨-25,0,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186373435 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e27e2e53-2bd4-5fd9-9c54-e7bc6e453f74" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨-1,-2,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373437} {:answer/id #uuid "fc30b76d-661e-5b7f-b41f-e7214a9e3f2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,0,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373438} {:answer/id #uuid "3c1c628f-d942-52cb-aa7e-76e397624b9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-1,-1,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373439} {:answer/id #uuid "3ec3b037-17fc-5106-a762-c7c3c5806797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373440} {:answer/id #uuid "99258556-2e23-5049-afc5-20a446995e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373441}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "99258556-2e23-5049-afc5-20a446995e6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373441} :answer-field/id #uuid "f18b47dd-75b2-5271-b7af-f2abcbd51dfb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186373436}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "28b318e9-60c2-5e57-acb1-0cc92a2b71d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-99583" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨2{e}^{t},{e}^{t},1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{{e}^{t}}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{5{e}^{2t}}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t},\\,-5{e}^{2t}⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(2{e}^{t})^{2}+{({e}^{t})}^{2}+{(-5{e}^{2t})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{4{e}^{2t}+{e}^{2t}+25{e}^{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}{e}^{t}}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{1+5{e}^{2t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}{e}^{t}}{5{e}^{2t}+1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{(5{e}^{2t}+1)^{3/2}}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,{e}^{t},\\,-5{e}^{2t}⟩}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}{e}^{t}}{5{e}^{2t}+1})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-5{e}^{t}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨2{e}^{t},{e}^{t},1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{5{e}^{2t}+1}}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-5{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(5{e}^{2t}+1)}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(5{e}^{2t}+1)}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t} & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & 1 \\\\ 2 & -5{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2{e}^{t} & {e}^{t} \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(5{e}^{2t}+1)}⟨-5{e}^{2t}-1,-(-10{e}^{2t}-2),2{e}^{t}-2{e}^{t}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(5{e}^{2t}+1)}⟨-(5{e}^{2t}+1),\\,2(5{e}^{2t}+1),\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨-1,2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486428 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34c9fe98-8103-5607-8dea-cf6c6d0a463f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨1,\\,0,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485863} {:answer/id #uuid "8b4c6ec2-89e0-57c5-8b8e-fa24254fc8c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,\\sqrt{2}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486012} {:answer/id #uuid "a373f55a-2df3-5bbb-8e0f-b55932c7ea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486059} {:answer/id #uuid "ab9e0421-550e-504a-b085-e1304399d534" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨0,\\,-1,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486074} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cf3825-effd-5b80-8c14-53fcf72aeb11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,\\,-2,\\,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486216}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a373f55a-2df3-5bbb-8e0f-b55932c7ea43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486059} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e34d722-fc15-5dc1-942d-021554bfeb73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486284}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b10a522e-2ca7-50dc-98ce-c79fed01cd4f" :question/math-academy-id "q-99651" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨2t,\\,2,\\,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2t}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{10}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}},\\,-\\frac{8t}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}},\\,\\frac{4t}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{(5)^{2}+(-4t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{25+16{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{20{t}^{2}+25} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{4{t}^{2}+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{2}{(4{t}^{2}+5)^{3/2}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩}{(\\frac{2\\sqrt{5}}{4{t}^{2}+5})}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨2t,2,-1⟩\\times \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}\\sqrt{4{t}^{2}+5}}⟨5,\\,-4t,\\,2t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2t & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & -4t & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ -4t & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}2t & 2 \\\\ 5 & -4t\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}⟨4t-4t,-(4{t}^{2}+5),-8{t}^{2}-10⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}(4{t}^{2}+5)}⟨0,\\,-(4{t}^{2}+5),\\,-2(4{t}^{2}+5)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}⟨0,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186486433 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166837 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d895a2-73eb-5141-b56d-48090debf57b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the General Binormal Vector to a Curve Given the Unit Tangent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c824f8b-b12d-596a-b458-0b38eb6a5d3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,1,\\,-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485847} {:answer/id #uuid "36129af3-9d71-53a7-ab78-a9f6e3fc98d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485867} {:answer/id #uuid "477f2e8f-f5d1-50d8-aa98-26b5ffbf9d75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}⟨-\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,1,\\,\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485896} {:answer/id #uuid "7074b204-75cd-52eb-8138-272ab4f76fd3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485958} {:answer/id #uuid "bebd21ce-52e7-5d1e-9493-b2bc0f6b6c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,1,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bebd21ce-52e7-5d1e-9493-b2bc0f6b6c02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,1,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486104} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dfc3adb-1e75-5b3f-be5e-d82fddc905b5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186486242}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "bb6bca21-eef1-511a-9545-14146c32b845" :question/math-academy-id "q-99652" :question/problem "Find the binormal vector to the curve $r(t)$ at an arbitrary point, given that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),2\\sqrt{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $T$ denotes the unit tangent vector." :question/worked-solution "The binormal vector is given by\n\n$$\nB(t)=T(t)\\times N(t),\n$$\n\nwhere the principal normal vector $N(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nN(t)=\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we find the principal normal $N(t).$ To do this, we calculate ${T}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\sqrt{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩ \\\\ ‖{T}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1))^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\sqrt{{cos}^{2}⁡(t+1)+{sin}^{2}⁡(t+1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we normalize ${T}^{′}(t)$ and obtain the principal normal to the curve:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}N(t) & =\\frac{{T}^{′}(t)}{‖{T}^{′}(t)‖}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩}{(\\frac{1}{3})}=⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we calculate the binormal vector, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(t) & =T(t)\\times N(t) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),2\\sqrt{2},\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩\\times ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1),\\,0,\\,-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\,\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1) & 2\\sqrt{2} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) & 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\text{ }\\left|\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{2} & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) \\\\ 0 & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,i-\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,j+\\left|\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1) & 2\\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1) & 0\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k\\text{ }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1)-0,-(-{sin}^{2}⁡(t+1)-{cos}^{2}⁡(t+1)),0-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t+1),\\,1,\\,-2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t+1)⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
